@startuml metadata_runtime_directory_mapping
title Metadata to CampusAgent Runtime Directory

' Source evidence:
' pi-mono packages/coding-agent/src/core/skills.ts: Skill, loadSkillFromFile, formatSkillsForPrompt
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/context/ContextFileLoader.java: loadSystemPrompt
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/session/AgentSession.java: loadSkills
' Observed behavior: pi and pi-mono-java discover Skill metadata from SKILL.md frontmatter.
' Java divergence: the target compiler materializes only one controlled Agent directory.
' Target design: the Managed loader reads .campusagent only; legacy code keeps .campusclaw.
' Target design: RuntimeSessionStore persists Session state in a shared database.
' Target design: Agent and Model IDs use resource prefixes plus 24 alphanumeric characters.
' Design reason: raw case-sensitive Agent IDs require a case-sensitive root and collision guard.
' Design reason: keep Agent-specific disclosure local while Managers remain runtime authorities.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  BorderColor #475569
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #EFF6FF
  BorderColor #2563EB
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam file {
  BackgroundColor #F0FDF4
  BorderColor #16A34A
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam ArrowColor #475569

rectangle "Resolved metadata input" as Input {
  rectangle "AGENT\nid, system_prompt\nmodels, bindings, policy" as AgentMetadata
  rectangle "SKILL\nname, description, content\nskill and tool bindings" as SkillMetadata
  rectangle "TOOL\nid, name, description\nschema, source, permission" as ToolMetadata
}

rectangle "Runtime bundle compiler" as Compiler {
  rectangle "Validate versions, IDs,\ndependency closure,\ncase-fold conflicts and policy" as Validate
  rectangle "Render prompt and\nSkill resources" as Render
  rectangle "Publish Agent directory\natomically" as Publish
}

rectangle "Controlled Agent directory\ncase-sensitive file system\n<agent-runtime-root>/<agent-id>/" as AgentDirectory {
  file ".campusagent/SYSTEM.md\nAgent instructions\nDirect Agent tool summaries" as SystemFile
  file ".campusagent/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md\nFrontmatter and Skill content" as SkillFile
  file ".campusagent/skills/<skill-name>/references/tools.json\nDirect Skill tool summaries" as SkillToolsFile
}

database "Agent metadata authority\nAgent model and binding policy" as AgentAuthority
database "Tool Manager authority\nTool schema, status,\npermission and execution" as ToolManager
database "Model Manager authority\nModel descriptor,\nallowlist and invocation" as ModelManager
database "RuntimeSessionStore\nSession, Message, RunRecord,\nhistory sequence and revisions" as SessionStore

AgentMetadata --> Validate
SkillMetadata --> Validate
ToolMetadata --> Validate
Validate --> Render
Render --> Publish
Publish --> SystemFile : system_prompt and direct tools
Publish --> SkillFile : name, description and content
Publish --> SkillToolsFile : direct Skill tools

AgentMetadata ..> AgentAuthority : publish metadata
ToolMetadata ..> ToolManager : publish executable definition
AgentMetadata ..> ModelManager : authorize model ids
AgentDirectory ..> SessionStore : pinned bundle revision

note right of SkillToolsFile
Only tool_id, name and description.
Schemas stay in Tool Manager.
Child Skill tools are not merged.
end note

note left of AgentDirectory
agent_id = agent_ + 24 alphanumeric characters
model_id = model_ + 24 alphanumeric characters
Compare IDs byte-for-byte.
Reject Agent ID case-fold collisions.
Verify directory and manifest identity.
end note
@enduml

@startuml managed_session_context_assembly
title Managed Multi-Agent Session and Context Assembly

' Source evidence:
' pi-mono packages/ai/src/types.ts: Context
' pi-mono packages/coding-agent/src/core/system-prompt.ts: buildSystemPrompt
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/session/AgentSession.java: initialize
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/SessionPool.java: getOrCreate
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ServerMode.java: websocket route
' pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ChatWebSocketHandler.java: handle
' pi-mono-java modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/loop/AgentLoop.java: invokeModel, toLlmTools
' Observed behavior: Java currently reads conversation_id during Upgrade and uses one base cwd.
' Java divergence: v2 authenticates Upgrade and maps closed Frames to a server-side SessionTransport.
' Architecture change: ManagedSessionTransport owns logical connection state; WebSocket is an adapter.
' Target design: globally unique session_id is the only SessionPool key; tenant and user stay upstream.
' Target design: a wss URI starts establishment; HTTP 101 establishes WebSocket transport.
' Target design: HTTP Upgrade and the first connect RequestFrame are separate protocol phases.
' Target design: trusted Gateway authentication and user-IP affinity precede agent-service.
' Target design: one Pod owns one active connection generation per Session.
' Target design: database history is authoritative; no target Session JSONL is generated.
' Design reason: isolate prompt, model, tool, persistence, and run recovery across Agents.

