participant "ChatWebSocketAdapter" as WS
participant "ManagedSessionPool" as Pool
participant "ManagedRunHub" as Hub
participant "Client reducer" as Reducer
database "RuntimeSessionStore\ndatabase history" as History

opt browser product
  Browser -> Client : upstream browser protocol\nout of Runtime scope
end

Client -> WS : establish wss through trusted Gateway\n/agent-service/v1/ws/chat
WS --> Client : HTTP 101
Client -> WS : req connect create or resume
WS -> Pool : bind session and agent
Pool -> Hub : atomic snapshot and cursor
Hub --> Pool : active_run or null
Pool --> WS : connect result
WS --> Client : res connect payload first
Client -> Reducer : enter sync and buffer post-snapshot events

alt idle session
  Client -> WS : req chat.send\ntext, attachments, or both\nand idempotency key
  WS -> Pool : persist user message and\natomically reserve run
  Pool --> WS : run_id and user_message_id
  WS --> Client : res chat.send before origin events
  Client -> Reducer : reconcile optimistic user message
  Hub --> WS : run, message, and tool events
  WS --> Client : typed EventFrames
  Client -> Reducer : verify seq and run_seq\nthen reduce by content_index
  WS --> Client : message.completed\nthen run.completed
  Client -> Reducer : replace partial message\nthen clear active run
else active session
  Client -> WS : req chat.send
  WS --> Client : res error RUN_ACTIVE
end

alt sequence gap or recoverable close
  Client -> Client : backoff and open new socket generation
  Client -> WS : req connect mode resume
  WS -> Pool : increment connection generation\nand replace the old same-Pod socket
  WS -> Hub : atomic snapshot and cursor
  Hub --> WS : run_seq N, history_seq H, frozen model/thinking,\npartial message, open contents, active tools
  WS --> Client : res connect snapshot first
  Hub --> WS : events with run_seq greater than N
  WS --> Client : post-snapshot EventFrames may arrive
  Client -> Reducer : validate connection seq and buffer
  Client -> WS : req chat.history(run_id, through H)
  WS -> History : read prior run messages and tool results
  History --> WS : history through watermark
  WS --> Client : res history
  Client -> Reducer : apply history, snapshot, and open state
  Client -> Reducer : release buffered events in run_seq order
else run ended while offline
  Client -> WS : req chat.history
  WS -> History : read messages and run records
  History --> WS : ordered history items
  WS --> Client : res authoritative history
  Client -> Reducer : reconcile by message_id and run_id
end

opt Pod restarted
  Client -> WS : resume, then req chat.history
  WS -> History : load last complete blocks and terminal records
  History --> WS : interrupted Message and RunRecord
  WS --> Client : authoritative interrupted history
  Client -> Reducer : mark the old response interrupted;\ndo not invent an unfinished tail
end

note over Browser,Client
Browser authentication and transport are upstream concerns.
The browser does not hold Runtime service credentials.
Attachment upload also belongs to mate-service.
end note

note over Client,Reducer
Protocol v2 always uses typed structured delta.
Only full_thinking is capability-negotiated.
Suppressed thinking updates use redacted placeholders.
Request id selects the pending payload decoder.
State-changing responses precede causal events.
end note
@enduml

@startuml managed_attachment_reference_lifecycle
title Managed attachment OBS-backed reference lifecycle

' Source evidence (pi-mono fc85bdd88be93b1e9a6b6bcfa41c684282ec79cc):
' packages/agent/src/agent.ts, prompt(), lines 336-395
' packages/ai/src/types.ts, ImageContent, lines 345-349
' Source evidence (pi-mono-java 1f7a5423219edfa4519d8719f1cc8a188ed72873):
' modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/types/UserMessage.java, lines 20-31
' modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/types/ContentBlock.java, lines 17-24
' modules/ai/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/ai/types/ImageContent.java, lines 9-18
' docs/plans/ws-chat-followups.md, lines 12-37
' Observed behavior: both baselines can carry inline image content but do not
' define a generic attachment_id or an external Attachment Service.
' Target design: mate-service streams original bytes to shared OBS, records
' authority and integrity metadata in shared openGauss, and exposes fixed HTTP
' upload, batch resolve, and content streaming APIs.
' Design reason: keep large-object transfer off the Chat control plane, support
' cross-Pod reads without local files, prevent metadata forgery, and retain
' reproducible public metadata snapshots in Runtime history.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #334155
  LifeLineBorderColor #64748B
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  ParticipantBorderColor #475569
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
  GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}

actor "End user" as User
participant "CampusMate client" as Client
participant "mate-service\nAttachment Service" as Attach
participant "background worker" as Worker
database "openGauss\nmetadata ledger" as DB
database "private OBS\ncontent store" as OBS
participant "mate-service\nRuntime client" as Upstream
participant "ChatWebSocketAdapter" as WS
participant "ManagedSessionTransport" as Transport
database "RuntimeSessionStore" as Store
participant "AttachmentInputAssembler" as Assembler
participant "Model Manager Provider" as Model

User -> Client : select one file
Client -> Attach : POST /v1/sessions/{session_id}/attachments\nmultipart file + X-Attachment-Size\nPrefer respond-async or wait=N
Attach -> Attach : authorize user and session;\nrequire size 1..20 MiB
Attach -> Attach : generate opaque attachment_id\nand random internal object key
Attach -> DB : INSERT UPLOADING metadata
DB --> Attach : committed
Attach -> OBS : put(objectKey, bounded stream, declared length)
Attach -> Attach : count bytes, verify file-part EOF,\nand compute SHA-256 with backpressure

alt upload failed or actual size mismatch
  Attach -> OBS : delete possible residual object
  Attach -> DB : mark FAILED
  Attach --> Client : bounded HTTP error
else OBS write succeeded
  OBS --> Attach : ETag and completion
  Attach -> DB : update PROCESSING, actual size,\ndigest and internal ETag
  Attach --> Client : 202 + Location + Retry-After\nunless wait reaches READY
  Worker -> DB : claim short scan lease for PROCESSING
  Worker -> OBS : open random object key as stream
  OBS --> Worker : bounded byte stream
  Worker -> Worker : verify size and digest;\nsniff MIME and scan security;\nnever execute JavaScript
  Worker -> DB : mark READY, BLOCKED, or FAILED
  Client -> Attach : GET /v1/sessions/{session_id}/attachments/{attachment_id}
  Attach -> DB : read authorized public state
  DB --> Attach : status and public metadata
  Attach --> Client : 200 attachment resource
end

User -> Client : send text, attachments, or both
Client -> Upstream : application chat request
Upstream -> WS : RequestFrame chat.send\nordered attachment_ids + idempotency_key
WS -> Transport : typed SessionRequest + auth context
Transport -> Store : lookup accepted idempotency result

alt accepted result exists with the same payload
  Store --> Transport : original run_id and user_message_id
  Transport --> WS : accepted result
  WS --> Upstream : ResponseFrame before causal events
else first attempt
  Transport -> Transport : acquire Session single-writer guard;\nreject a different active run
  Transport -> Attach : POST /internal/v1/attachments:resolve\nservice token + session_id + ordered IDs
  Attach -> DB : short transaction: lock all rows;\nrequire same session, READY,\nnot deleted, and not expired
  alt any attachment is invalid
    DB --> Attach : rollback all changes
    Attach --> Transport : one safe batch error
    Transport --> WS : failed ResponseFrame; no run
  else all attachments are valid
    Attach -> DB : atomically set referenced=true,\npreserve first referenced_at, expires_at=NULL
    DB --> Attach : committed public snapshots
    Attach --> Transport : ordered id, filename, media type,\nsize, and SHA-256
    Transport -> Store : commit user Message snapshots,\nidempotency result, run,\nand active run state
    Store --> Transport : run_id and user_message_id
    Transport --> WS : accepted result
    WS --> Upstream : ResponseFrame before run events

    Transport -> Assembler : ordered public snapshots
    loop each attachment
      Assembler -> Attach : GET /internal/v1/sessions/{session_id}/\nattachments/{attachment_id}/content\nwith expected SHA-256
      Attach -> DB : require READY, referenced,\nsame session, and matching digest
      DB --> Attach : internal random object key
      Attach -> OBS : open(objectKey)
      OBS --> Attach : original byte stream
      Attach --> Assembler : bounded proxy stream
      Assembler -> Assembler : verify length and SHA-256;\nconstruct provider-neutral input
    end
    Assembler -> Model : optional text plus ordered attachments
    Model --> Transport : model stream
  end
end

group Public deletion
  Client -> Attach : DELETE unreferenced attachment
  Attach -> DB : conditional update to DELETING
  alt attachment is already referenced
    DB --> Attach : conflict
    Attach --> Client : 409 ATTACHMENT_REFERENCED
  else deletion accepted
    DB --> Attach : DELETING
    Attach --> Client : 202
    Worker -> OBS : delete object with retry
    Worker -> DB : mark DELETED tombstone
  end
end

group Session deletion
  Upstream -> Transport : stop or abort Runtime Session
  Upstream -> Attach : delete all attachments for session_id
  Attach -> DB : mark all remaining rows DELETING
  Worker -> OBS : delete each object with retry
  Worker -> DB : retain permanent DELETED tombstones
end

note over Client,OBS
Clients never access OBS directly.
No presigned upload or deterministic object path is part of v1.
Upload retries create a new attachment_id.
The file body exists only in OBS; openGauss stores metadata.
end note

note over Attach,DB
The attachment row is a one-way Session binding.
Referenced rows clear expires_at and cannot be deleted alone.
If Runtime persistence later fails, conservative retention lasts
until Session deletion; there is no release protocol.
end note

note over WS,Attach
The WebSocket carries only ordered attachment_ids.
agent-service never receives object keys, OBS URLs, ETags,
storage credentials, or a complete in-memory file.
end note

note over Store,Model
Runtime history stores exactly attachment_id, filename,
media_type, size_bytes, and SHA-256.
File bodies are untrusted user data.
end note
@enduml
